    "created_at": "2021-05-21T22:28:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-21T22:29:08Z",
    "body": "I don't think manufacturer and product name introduce any privacy concerns. There's nothing there you'd learn that you wouldn't from a USB vendor or product ID, unless the product has a special need for that information, in which case it's about functionality not privacy. Serial number, yeah, it's a real concern. Usually all you really need there is any (even origin specific) unique ID to keep track of which device is which. I work around the lack of this on WebHID right now, but it is NOT pretty how I'm having to do it :)",
