    "created_at": "2021-05-22T10:51:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-22T10:51:10Z",
    "body": "To be fair, it'll only be more useful than the product ID for /them/. Normally, different products have different product ID. Sharing a product ID and using product name to differentiate is a mistake -- product name can even be localized, so it's not the appropriate place to differentiate a product. But I do understand. Once you have tens or hundreds of thousands of something out in the real world, whether it was a mistake or not doesn't tend to matter. It's just got to be made to work.\r\n\r\nHow are the people who used Product Name in this version doing it now for their serial device? Surely they have a Windows client, maybe they can share the code they are using to make it happen.\r\n\r\nFWIW USB Product Version should be significantly easier than any of these. On every OS it'll be in the same structure giving you the VID and PID.",
